Subject: Write libadwaita's colours from the KDE scheme into colors.css

libadwaita ignores the GTK theme and draws only from its own named colours,
so with the Breeze names alone a libadwaita program keeps Adwaita's palette
under every KDE colour scheme and follows only the accent and the light/dark
preference the settings portal carries. The kded module now also writes
accent, status, window, view, header bar, sidebar, card, dialog, popover and
thumbnail colours from the same KColorScheme sets it already reads: as named
colours for both GTK versions, and for GTK 4 as the CSS custom properties
(--accent-bg-color and the rest) that libadwaita 1.6 and later reads instead.
GTK 3 cannot parse custom properties, so its colors.css gets the names only.
A status colour that fills a button takes the view's background or its text
on top, whichever has the higher contrast ratio against it.

--- a/kded/config_editor/custom_css.cpp
+++ b/kded/config_editor/custom_css.cpp
